NAME
    cores - list, download, install, update, roll back, remove, and verify
            hosted libretro cores

SYNOPSIS
    cores ls [--installed|--available|--updates|--unsupported] [<console>]
    cores info <core>
    cores fetch
    cores get <core>...
    cores update [<core>...]
    cores rollback <core>
    cores rm <core>...
    cores verify [<core>...]
    cores approve <core>
    cores default <console> [<engine>]
    cores default --game <path> [<engine>|-]
    cores wait [cores<n>]

DESCRIPTION
    Manages the hosted libretro cores under /Cores/libretro through the
    emusen.library service. EmuSen hosts one libretro core for each
    console it supports natively plus Saturn and Dreamcast: pcee2
    (PlayStation 2), flycast (Dreamcast, Naomi, Atomiswave), snes9x,
    nestopia, genesis_plus_gx (Genesis, Sega CD, Master System, SG-1000),
    picodrive (32X), mupen64plus_next, sameboy, mednafen_psx_hw, and
    mednafen_saturn. Only hosted cores are offered for download; any other
    core placed in /Cores/libretro is listed as unsupported with a reason.

    Each console keeps its own native core as default, except PlayStation
    2 where pcee2 is the default while Sapphire is under development. Use
    'cores default' to change the engine for a console or a single game.

    A core is always named by its file stem (for example, pcee2 for
    pcee2_libretro.so), which also names its folder under /Cores/libretro.
    No network access happens unless explicitly requested by 'fetch',
    'get', or 'update'.

    'cores ls' prints one space-separated line per core: state, console,
    id, source, version, size, and licence (empty fields as '-', internal
    spaces as '_', licence as the rest of the line). States are:

        installed     Downloaded and matching the cached index.
        update        Downloaded, with a newer build in the index.
        available     Present in the cached catalogue, not downloaded.
        unsupported   Cannot run on EmuSen's host (for example, OpenGL-
                      only or unmapped system); see 'cores info'.
        added         Folder placed in /Cores/libretro manually without a
                      NOTICE; never removed by 'cores rm'.

    'cores info' prints key: value metadata (names, authors, licence,
    version, build, systems, notes, permissions, required or optional
    firmware paths, source URL, index CRC-32, and for installed cores the
    SHA-256 and fetch date).

OPTIONS
    ls [--installed|--available|--updates|--unsupported] [<console>]
        List cores from the cached catalogue, optionally filtered by one
        state flag and one console name.

    info <core>
        Print cached and installed details for <core>.

    fetch
        Download libretro's core info archive (assets/frontend/info.zip)
        and the platform nightly index from buildbot.libretro.com over
        HTTPS (system certificate store, cross-host redirects refused).
        Replaces /Cores/libretro/.catalogue/ only after validation.

    get <core>...
        Download, verify, stage under /Cores/libretro/.staging/, and
        atomically install each named core. Prints the SHA-256 to approve.

    update [<core>...]
        Install newer builds offered by the cached index for all outdated
        installed cores or the named cores. Moves the prior build to
        /Cores/libretro/.previous/ so it can be restored with rollback.

    rollback <core>
        Swap <core> with its kept previous build in .previous/. A second
        rollback switches back. Both builds retain their approvals.

    rm <core>...
        Remove each downloaded core and its kept previous build, revoking
        their approvals. Saves, settings, and manually added folders
        without a NOTICE are untouched.

    verify [<core>...]
        Check installed cores against their NOTICE hashes and refresh
        EmuSen's libretro host and proxy copies if updated. Prints one
        line per core starting with ok, refreshed, changed, or added.

    approve <core>
        Record trust-on-first-download approval for the installed build's
        SHA-256. Must be typed interactively at the prompt; scripts,
        command substitutions, and pipes are refused.

    default <console> [<engine>]
        Print or set the default engine for <console>.

    default --game <path> [<engine>|-]
        Print, set, or clear ('-') the per-game engine override for <path>.

    wait [cores<n>]
        Follow a background core job until completion.

VERIFICATION AND APPROVAL
    Every download from 'get' or 'update' is checked over HTTPS (no off-
    host redirects), index CRC-32, zip shape (single <core>_libretro.so
    member, no traversal or symlinks), inflated size (512 MB cap), member
    CRC-32/length, host CPU architecture, and SHA-256 written to NOTICE.

    Downloaded builds never execute until approved with 'cores approve'.
    Because libretro does not sign builds, approval pins execution to the
    exact SHA-256 hash; any change requires re-approval. 'cores default',
    'cores approve', and approval revocation require the emusen.settings
    service (see modules(7)). Only one mutating operation on
    /Cores/libretro may run at a time across all EmuSen processes.

JOBS
    Long-running commands continue in the background as cores<n>. Use
    ps(1) to inspect progress, 'cores wait' to reattach, and kill(1) to
    cancel.

EXAMPLES
    cores fetch
    cores ls --available
    cores ls --updates | wc -l
    cores ls --installed | grep GPL
    cores info pcee2
    cores get pcee2
    cores update
    cores rollback pcee2
    cores verify | grep -v '^ok'
    cores approve pcee2
    cores default "PlayStation 2" Sapphire
    cores default --game /Games/ps2/jak.chd -
    cores rm pcee2
    for c in $(cores ls --updates | awk '{print $3}'); do cores info $c; done

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command succeeded (or detached cleanly to a background job).
    1   Invalid arguments, unknown or refused core, missing service,
        verification failure, or network error.

SEE ALSO
    modules(7), trust(1), chd(1), pkg(1), ps(1), kill(1), hier(7)
